<%# Lo que se ve cuando `Bali.rich_text_editor_enabled` está en false, que es el default del
    paquete. Sin esto el preview contesta 200 con el body vacío y se lee como un componente
    roto (#844). %>
<div class="space-y-4">
  <%= render Bali::Alert::Component.new(
    title: 'This preview renders nothing on purpose',
    color: :warning,
    icon: true
  ) do %>
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <p>
        <code>Bali::RichTextEditor::Component</code> defines
        <code>render?</code> as <code>Bali.rich_text_editor_enabled</code>, which the package
        ships as <code>false</code>. With the flag off the component emits no markup at all
        &mdash; not even its wrapper &mdash; so an empty preview here is the flag, not a defect.
      </p>
      <p>
        The flag exists because this editor is the only reason the package declares
        roughly thirty-five <code>@tiptap/*</code> optional peers plus <code>lowlight</code> and
        <code>highlight.js</code>. Rendering it without those installed gives a dead
        <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>, so it is opt-in.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%= render Bali::Alert::Component.new(
    title: 'Deprecated in v3, removed in v4',
    color: :info,
    icon: true
  ) do %>
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <p>
        Use <code>Bali::BlockEditor::Component</code> instead. It covers the same ground on a
        maintained stack and reads and writes the same HTML through
        <code>html_content:</code> / <code>format: :html</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <%= render Bali::Link::Component.new(
          name: 'Open the BlockEditor previews',
          href: '/lookbook/inspect/bali/block_editor/default',
          variant: :primary,
          size: :sm
        ) %>
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-base-content/70">
    <p>
      To see this component rendered anyway &mdash; to check a migration, say &mdash; boot the
      dummy with the flag on:
    </p>
    <pre class="bg-base-200 rounded-box p-3 overflow-x-auto"><code>ENABLE_RICH_TEXT_EDITOR=1 bin/dev</code></pre>
    <p>
      In a host application the equivalent is
      <code>config.rich_text_editor_enabled = true</code>, and it only makes sense once the
      TipTap peers are installed.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
